<title>USA: Whitestone acquires Proformix Inc.</title>
<headline>Whitestone acquires Proformix Inc.</headline>
<dateline>BRANCHBURG, N.J. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Whitestone Industries Inc said it is acquiring Proformix Inc, which designs, manufactures and markets research-based ergonomic products for computers.</p>
<p>Terms of the stock-for-stock exchange were not disclosed. Along with the acquisition, Whitestone said it has changed its name to Proformix Systems Inc.</p>
<p>Proformix Inc was a privately held company based in New Jersey.</p>
<p>Proformix Systems Inc's primary product is a patented keyboarding system that seeks to substantially reduce the risk factors associated with carpal tunnel syndrome and other repetitive stress injuries.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
